                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 23pt 0pt 5pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Under general supervision, the OC Fair &amp; Event Center Heavy Equipment Mechanic construct, repair and maintain automotive and construction&nbsp;equipment. May lead workers to perform a wide variety of tasks.</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&nbsp;</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 0pt 17pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Responsible for the maintenance of various equipment and, completes scheduled and unscheduled repairs as directed by the department supervisor.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 19pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Repairs and maintains small and heavy equipment (forklifts electric carts, bobcat, skip loaders, water truck, dump truck, lawnmowers, blowers, hedgers, pressure</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">washers, whackers, concrete saws, chain saws and light duty trucks).</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 7pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Repairs and maintains automotive equipment, including engines, brakes, wheel and tire service, transmission and differential service and repairs, electrical&nbsp; component replacement and repairs, and minor body and paint repairs.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 13pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Troubleshoots engines, transmissions, hydraulic systems and electrical systems in the automotive and heavy equipment.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 23pt 0pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Operates and performs required inspections of equipment, vehicles facilities and systems as identified.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 40pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Inspects equipment problems, determines the extent of the repairs and takes appropriate corrective action.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 12pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Ensures that all applicable laws, rules and regulations are complied with during the operation and maintenance of equipment including carts, forklifts and other miscellaneous equipment.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 5pt; line-height: 13pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Removes from service and reports unsafe equipment and vehicles.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 20pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Serve as a lead for Maintenance Workers and seasonal employees in day-to-day assignments by instructing and guiding their work.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 24pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 1.175;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Instructs operators in the proper operation and servicing equipment to ensure all equipment is used properly and safely.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 5pt; line-height: 11pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Maintains records and reports of all training and maintenance.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 0pt 10pt 0pt 23pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Operates and maintains mechanic shop equipment, inventory, tools and machinery used in the repair and maintenance of heavy maintenance and construction equipment.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 18pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Estimates, orders and procures materials, parts and supplies required to maintain equipment and accomplish work.</span></p><p style="font-size: 11pt; text-align: left; text-indent: -18pt; margin: 1pt 31pt 0pt 23pt; line-height: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">•&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Perform miscellaneous minor building construction, electrical maintenance and repair work and equipment.</span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25352921&name=MaintenanceMechanic.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
