    <div id="pnlDesirableQualifications" class="jcBand">
	
        <h3 class="postingHeader">Desirable Qualifications</h3>
        <div class="postingContent">
            In addition to evaluating each candidate's relative ability, as demonstrated by quality and breadth of experience, the following factors will provide the basis for competitively evaluating each candidate:
        </div>
        <div class="postingContent">
            <ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Skill in mechanical repair, adjustment, and fabrication of special equipment.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to communicate effectively, read and write English at a level required for&nbsp;successful job performance.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to fabricate, repair and make adjustments to various equipment and systems (i.e., heavy construction and maintenance equipment, gas- and diesel-powered trucks, etc.).</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to perform welding, install and test pumps, motors and similar equipment.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to work from drawings and sketches and make sketches of broken parts for replacement.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to estimate repair costs and make repairs in the field without supervision.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to proficiently operate hand tools/power tools and heavy equipment (drivers, screw guns, skip loader, fork-lift, trencher, tillers, sander, band saw, airless sprayer, rototiller, grinders, tractor, power snakes, etc.) and other equipment to ensure safe and proper operations of the tools and equipment during the performance of daily assignments.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to safely lift up to 50 pounds, using proper body mechanics, in order to complete construction, maintenance and repair assignments.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to obtain certifications for powered industrial vehicles (e.g., forklifts, hand lifts, articulating boom lifts) to perform assigned duties independently.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability to perform physical activities that require considerable use of limbs and body parts, such as, but not limited to: climbing, crawling, lifting, balancing, walking, stooping, digging and handling of materials, in order to complete the task in a safe manner.<br /></span></li><li><span style="text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 12pt;">Ability to be open to change and effectively adapt to constant change in work assignments and projects.</span></li></ul>
        </div>
    
</div>

    

